From 318d44262d6ad5b19b51800791ed92bbf487578c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hang(Harry) Gao <GaohRyan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 23:00:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 13/19] terrain: evaluation (per-tile windows with the climb
 actually done), scan for the policy in every eval script, box-only terrain by
 default

- supermimic/eval/terrain_eval.py: one fixed-length window per env on chosen tiles; not fallen, completed with the
  climb done (>= 70 % of the reference path's height change when the path crosses at least two risers), fixed-
  denominator return, progress. The same loop runs under mjlab (scripts/eval_terrain.py) and in the plain-MuJoCo
  stand-in of the main repository.
- sensor tests: flat-ground scan (--scan flat), scaled relief (--scan-relief).
- eval_fullclip_traj / eval_push / benchmark / play / record_rollout / diag_drift give a scan policy the flat-ground
  scan on the plane.
- curriculum: a motion bin no flat env has visited yet is measured against the mean flat-tile reward.
- reset placement: sole sample points cover the capsule radius.
- terrain: slope and rough height-field tiles off by default (in plain MuJoCo foot capsules behave differently on a
  flat height field than on the flat box tile); stairs up / down / uneven + flat.
- tests: lifts, reset placement, origins, actor scan, checkpoint and optimizer expansion, curriculum rules; conftest
  with stand-ins so that they run without the mjlab runtime; the stale recorder test fixed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
